## Working mode notes (for future agents)

> Owner profile, communication style, technical level. How to drive at the right granularity. Permissions when to ask vs. proceed.

{{OWNER_NAME}} is the product owner. {{COMMUNICATION_STYLE}}. {{TECHNICAL_LEVEL}}.

**Drive at the right granularity.** When {{OWNER_NAME}} approves a scope (a phase, a chunk), execute the WHOLE thing without asking at each sub-step. Check in at meaningful milestones, not per task. Ask permission for destructive/external actions, remote push/deploy, credentials, data migrations, real product forks where >1 answer is defensible, or genuine blockers. Local commits are OK when meaningful and verified, unless the project says otherwise.

**Be proactive.** Add small adjacent polish, surface gotchas, propose improvements at milestone reports. Senior-engineer behavior, not task-runner.

**Bigger slices than they look on paper.** Group fine-grained slices into chunks; each chunk is one milestone, not one task.
